## 1. Aim

The aim of this laboratory was to capture and analyse network traffic generated within the ICDFA virtual laboratory using Wireshark, and to understand how devices communicate across a TCP/IP network. The exercise covered Ethernet and IPv4 addressing, ARP, ICMP, DNS and TCP, and ended with saving the capture as evidence.

## 2. Objectives

- Examine Ethernet frame communication.
- Investigate ARP requests and replies.
- Analyse the relationship between IPv4 and MAC addresses.
- Capture and analyse ICMP traffic.
- Observe DNS name resolution traffic.
- Analyse TCP connection traffic and the three-way handshake.
- Save the capture in PCAPNG format as evidence.
- Develop packet analysis and troubleshooting skills using Wireshark.


